{"text": "Abebe Family Law, P.C. - PRIVILEGED AND CONFIDENTIAL - File 26-AD-0173\n\nStepparent Adoption - Notes to File\nAttorney: Corinne Abebe (Atty. Reg. No. 44718). Conference: Thursday, May 14, 2026, both clients in the office, about 70 minutes.\n1. Petitioner (stepfather)\nNathaniel J. Vanterpool (\"Nate\"), born July 6, 1986 in Wichita, Kansas. SSN 359-10-7624. Colorado driver license 17-204-8831. Tooling engineer at Peakline Aerospace Fasteners, Inc. since 2019; salary $104,000 plus bonus. Married the mother on 09/18/2021. Has lived with the child since June 2020.\n2. Mother\nJocelyn Vanterpool, formerly Jocelyn Batista, DOB 12/01/1989. Dental hygienist, part time, about $38,500 a year. Cell 720-555-0142; jocelyn.vanterpool@mailhaven.example. Family home: 19044 East Girard Place, Aurora, CO 80013 (Arapahoe County).\n3. Child\nElias Batista Rourke, goes by Eli, born February 2, 2015 in Amarillo, Texas; he is 11 and in 5th grade at Cherry Creek Trail Elementary. Texas birth certificate, state file no. 142-15-018827. SSN ends -2246. Pediatrician: Aurora Meadows Pediatric Group. Eli has ADHD and takes methylphenidate ER 27 mg on school days. He is 11, so his written consent is not required (it would be at 12), but the court will want to hear from him. He calls Nate \"Dad\" and asked on his own whether his name can be Elias Batista Vanterpool. Not an Indian child; ICWA inquiry made of both sides of the family, none claimed.\n4. Birth father\nShane Rourke, DOB 10/23/1987. Never married to the mother; on the birth certificate. Last contact with Elias was a phone call at Christmas 2022. Last-known address c/o 4417 SW 45th Avenue, Lot 12, Amarillo, TX 79109; his mother there says he \"comes and goes.\" Child support order out of Potter County, Texas, cause no. D-1-FM-16-004418: $415 a month, nothing paid since March 2023, arrears about $16,600. Mr. Rourke served 14 months in a Texas state jail for possession of a controlled substance (released 2021). Jocelyn does not want his record \"thrown at him\" if he will simply sign.\n5. Grounds\nIf Shane signs Form JDF 503 (consent), we proceed on consent. If he cannot be found or refuses: C.R.S. § 19-5-203(1)(d)(II), Abandonment for a year or more or Failure to pay reasonable Support for a year or more without cause. Servicemembers Civil Relief Act Affidavit needed either way; Jocelyn says he was never in the military.\n6. Background Checks\nFingerprints submitted 5/15; Colorado Bureau of Investigation and FBI results come back to the court directly. TRAILS (child abuse registry) check requested for both adults. Nate disclosed, before I asked, a 2011 misdemeanor DUI in Sedgwick County, Kansas, deferred and dismissed. Explanation goes with the Petition (Form JDF 501); not disqualifying under C.R.S. § 19-5-105.5.\n7. Home Study\nIf the court orders one: Columbine Family Assessments, LLC, evaluator Priscilla Nyberg, LCSW, 303.555.0166, flat $850. Ms. Nyberg will want to meet the maternal grandmother, Imelda Batista, who lives in the basement apartment and does after-school care. Imelda is a lawful permanent resident from Brazil; she worries about being fingerprinted. Told Jocelyn the registry check is by name and date of birth only (hers: 4 April 1962).\n8. Costs\nFlat Fee $3,200.00 (thirty-two hundred), half paid today by check no. 2291. Filing Fee $167. Publication, if needed, roughly $300. New birth certificate from Texas Vital Records $27.00.\n9. To Do\nDraft Petition and Consent; send Consent to Shane by certified mail and to shanerourke87@quickpost.example, the last email Jocelyn has for him.\nDiligent Search Affidavit if nothing back by June 15.\nAsk Arapahoe County District Court clerk for a hearing in late August so the Decree is in hand before 6th grade registration. Case number once filed will be in the form 2026JA000---.\nCalendar: Eli turns 12 on 2/2/2027. File well before then.\nCA", "kind": "Word document", "detail": "617 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["Corinne A